        "title": "Scientific Revolutions: Kuhn and Critics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Thomas Kuhn's Structure of Scientific Revolutions (1962) is the most influential work in\n20th-century philosophy/history of science. It introduced \"paradigm,\" \"normal science,\" and\n\"scientific revolution\" into common use. Its reception generated a rich debate: Lakatos,\nFeyerabend, Popper, and Laudan all responded."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md#003",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions, git-history:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions]",
        "canonical_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "current_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:intellectual-history:scientific-revolutions",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "intellectual-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "section": "intellectual-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Revolutions: Kuhn and Critics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n.===================================================================.\n!              MODELS OF SCIENTIFIC CHANGE                          !\n!                                                                   !\n!  CLASSICAL (Cumulative)       KUHN (Revolutionary)                !\n!  .=====================.      .=========================.         !\n!  ! Science adds to a   !      ! Normal science within   !         !\n!  ! growing body of     !      ! paradigm -> anomalies   !         !\n!  ! knowledge           !      ! -> crisis -> revolution !         !\n!  ! Errors corrected;   !      ! Paradigm shift:         !         !\n!  ! truths accumulate   !      ! incommensurable worlds  !         !\n!  .=====================.      .=========================.         !\n   !                                                                !\n   !  POPPER (Falsificationism)    LAKATOS (Research Programmes)    !\n!  .=====================.      .=========================.         !\n!  ! Science progresses  !      ! Hard core protected by  !         !\n!  ! by bold conjectures !      ! auxiliary belt          !         !\n!  ! and ruthless        !      ! Progressive vs.         !         !\n!  ! refutations         !      ! degenerative programmes !         !\n!  .=====================.      .=========================.         !\n   !                                                                !\n   !  FEYERABEND                   LAUDAN (Problem-Solving)         !\n!  .=====================.      .=========================.         !\n!  ! \"Against Method\":   !      ! Science solves          !         !\n!  ! No single method    !      ! conceptual and          !         !\n!  ! works for all       !      ! empirical problems      !         !\n!  ! science; \"anything  !      ! No convergence to truth !         !\n!  ! goes\" rhetorically  !      !                         !         !\n!  .=====================.      .=========================.         !\n.===================================================================.\n```"
    },
    {
