      "text": "### Paradigms"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md#007",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions, git-history:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions]",
        "canonical_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "current_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:intellectual-history:scientific-revolutions",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "intellectual-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "section": "intellectual-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Revolutions: Kuhn and Critics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  PARADIGM (Kuhn's central and most contested concept):\n  In narrow sense: an exemplary problem-solution that serves as model\n  for subsequent work. (Kuhn later preferred \"exemplar.\")"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md#008",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions, git-history:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions]",
        "canonical_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "current_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:intellectual-history:scientific-revolutions",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "intellectual-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "section": "intellectual-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Revolutions: Kuhn and Critics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "In broad sense (Masterman identified 21 senses): the entire constellation\n  of beliefs, values, techniques, and puzzle-solutions shared by a community.\n  (Kuhn later called this a \"disciplinary matrix.\")"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md#009",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions, git-history:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions]",
        "canonical_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "current_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:intellectual-history:scientific-revolutions",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "intellectual-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "section": "intellectual-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Revolutions: Kuhn and Critics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "KEY PROPERTIES:\n  1. Paradigms solve \"paradigmatic\" problems that define the field.\n  2. They are never fully articulated — tacit knowledge is crucial.\n  3. They are not \"proven\" before adoption; they are adopted because\n     they open up productive research directions."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md#010",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions, git-history:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions]",
        "canonical_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "current_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:intellectual-history:scientific-revolutions",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "intellectual-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "section": "intellectual-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Revolutions: Kuhn and Critics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "EXAMPLES:\n  Ptolemaic astronomy -> Copernican/Newtonian paradigm\n  Phlogiston chemistry -> Lavoisier's oxygen chemistry\n  Caloric theory of heat -> Thermodynamics\n  Classical mechanics -> Quantum mechanics\n  Newtonian gravity -> General Relativity\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md#011",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions, git-history:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions]",
        "canonical_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
