        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Revolutions: Kuhn and Critics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "### Normal Science"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md#012",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions, git-history:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions]",
        "canonical_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "current_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:intellectual-history:scientific-revolutions",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "intellectual-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "section": "intellectual-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Revolutions: Kuhn and Critics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  NORMAL SCIENCE: Research within an accepted paradigm.\n  The paradigm defines which problems are legitimate,\n  what counts as a solution, and what methods are appropriate."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md#013",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions, git-history:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions]",
        "canonical_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "current_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:intellectual-history:scientific-revolutions",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "intellectual-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "section": "intellectual-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Revolutions: Kuhn and Critics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "\"Puzzle-solving\": scientists solve pre-defined puzzles\n  (not open-ended problems) within the paradigm's framework."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md#014",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions, git-history:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions]",
        "canonical_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "current_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:intellectual-history:scientific-revolutions",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "intellectual-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "section": "intellectual-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Revolutions: Kuhn and Critics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "WHY \"PUZZLE\" NOT \"PROBLEM\":\n  A puzzle has a known solution; the challenge is to find it.\n  Normal science assumes the paradigm is right and tries to\n  make nature fit the paradigm's predictions."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md#015",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions, git-history:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions]",
        "canonical_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "current_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:intellectual-history:scientific-revolutions",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "intellectual-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "section": "intellectual-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Revolutions: Kuhn and Critics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "KEY FEATURE: Anomalies are NOT treated as refutations.\n  When experiment disagrees with theory: first, check the experiment.\n  Then, try auxiliary hypotheses. Only prolonged, serious anomalies\n  lead to crisis."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md#016",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions, git-history:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions]",
        "canonical_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "current_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:intellectual-history:scientific-revolutions",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "intellectual-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "section": "intellectual-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Revolutions: Kuhn and Critics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "EXAMPLE: Le Verrier calculated where a planet had to be to account\n  for anomalies in Uranus's orbit. The planet (Neptune) was found.\n  Normal science success: don't abandon the paradigm, find the planet.\n```"
    },
