        "root_concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "section": "intellectual-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Revolutions: Kuhn and Critics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Normal science\n       !\n       v  Accumulation of anomalies\n  Crisis (anomalies resist resolution)\n       !\n       v  Proliferation of competing theories\n  Revolution (paradigm replaced)\n       !\n       v  New normal science"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md#020",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions, git-history:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions]",
        "canonical_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "current_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:intellectual-history:scientific-revolutions",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "intellectual-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "section": "intellectual-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Revolutions: Kuhn and Critics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "WHAT TRIGGERS REVOLUTION:\n  Not a single anomaly, but a prolonged series that undermines\n  confidence in the paradigm.\n  New paradigm typically proposed by newcomers to the field,\n  not established practitioners (who have too much invested)."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md#021",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions, git-history:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions]",
        "canonical_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "current_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:intellectual-history:scientific-revolutions",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "intellectual-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "section": "intellectual-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Revolutions: Kuhn and Critics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "GESTALT SWITCH METAPHOR:\n  The shift in seeing is sudden and total.\n  Scientists who made the switch say the world looks different.\n  Kuhn: \"working in a different world\" after the revolution.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md#022",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
