        "title": "Scientific Revolutions: Kuhn and Critics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "### Incommensurability"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md#023",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions, git-history:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions]",
        "canonical_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "current_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:intellectual-history:scientific-revolutions",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "intellectual-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "section": "intellectual-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Revolutions: Kuhn and Critics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  INCOMMENSURABILITY: Paradigms before and after a revolution cannot be\n  directly compared on a common scale."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md#024",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions, git-history:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions]",
        "canonical_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "current_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:intellectual-history:scientific-revolutions",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "intellectual-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "section": "intellectual-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Revolutions: Kuhn and Critics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "TWO TYPES (Kuhn's later refinement):\n  1. METHODOLOGICAL: Different criteria for what counts as good science.\n     Newton vs. Aristotle used different notions of explanation."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md#025",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions, git-history:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions]",
        "canonical_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "current_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:intellectual-history:scientific-revolutions",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "intellectual-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "section": "intellectual-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Revolutions: Kuhn and Critics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "2. SEMANTIC: Key terms change meaning across paradigms.\n     \"Mass\" means different things in Newtonian and Einsteinian physics.\n     \"Oxygen\" in Lavoisier's chemistry is not the same concept as\n     Priestley's \"dephlogisticated air\" even though they refer to the same element."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md#026",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions, git-history:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions]",
        "canonical_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "current_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:intellectual-history:scientific-revolutions",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "intellectual-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "section": "intellectual-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Revolutions: Kuhn and Critics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "CONSEQUENCE: Paradigms cannot be rationally compared by appeal to\n  neutral, theory-independent evidence. Comparison requires translation,\n  and perfect translation is impossible."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md#027",
      "path": [
        "03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions, git-history:intellectual-history:03-scientific-revolutions]",
        "canonical_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "current_path": "intellectual-history/03-SCIENTIFIC-REVOLUTIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:intellectual-history:scientific-revolutions",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "intellectual-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[scientific, revolutions]",
        "section": "intellectual-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Scientific Revolutions: Kuhn and Critics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "CRITICS ARGUE:\n  If paradigms are fully incommensurable, how does Kuhn himself compare\n  Ptolemy and Copernicus? He must presuppose some common measure.\n  KUHN'S REPLY: Partial incommensurability; translation is imperfect but not impossible.\n```"
    }
